      "confidence": "medium",
      "description": "_currentPrice() reads a single pair's instantaneous reserves with no TWAP or staleness check, and isLiquidatable()/liquidate() use that price directly. An attacker can manipulate the pool's reserves within one transaction to make a healthy position appear liquidatable (or vice versa).",
      "evidence": [
        "function _currentPrice() internal view returns (uint256) {",
        "    (uint112 reserve0, uint112 reserve1, ) = collateralPair.getReserves();",
        "    return (uint256(reserve1) * 1e18) / uint256(reserve0);",
        "}"
